{
  "version": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Lab 2 — WeatherReading Model & ProcessWeather"
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "# Lab 2 — `WeatherReading` Model & `ProcessWeather` Action\n\nIn this lab, you will transform a raw JSON payload from the Open-Meteo weather API into a clean, typed reading on `campus/weather/reading`.\n\n### Cell 1: `WeatherReading` Model\nA **Model** defines the shape and data types of a message.\n- `COLLAPSED` means that when you publish this Model to a topic (like `campus/weather/reading`), the broker publishes **one flat JSON object** containing all 6 fields.\n- Each `ADD <TYPE> \"field\"` line declares a field name and how it is populated (`WITH TOPIC` copies a value published to a child sub-topic; `WITH TIMESTAMP \"UTC\"` stamps the current UTC time automatically).\n\nClick **▷** on the cell below to deploy `WeatherReading` first:"
    },
    {
      "kind": 2,
      "language": "lot",
      "value": "DEFINE MODEL WeatherReading COLLAPSED\n    ADD STRING \"station\" WITH \"campus-main\"\n    ADD DOUBLE \"temperature_c\" WITH TOPIC \"campus/weather/reading/temperature_c\"\n    ADD DOUBLE \"temperature_f\" WITH TOPIC \"campus/weather/reading/temperature_f\"\n    ADD DOUBLE \"wind_kmh\" WITH TOPIC \"campus/weather/reading/wind_kmh\"\n    ADD INT \"weather_code\" WITH TOPIC \"campus/weather/reading/weather_code\"\n    ADD STRING \"observed_at\" WITH TIMESTAMP \"UTC\"\n"
    },
    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "### Cell 2: `ProcessWeather` Action\nWhenever a raw JSON response arrives on `campus/weather/raw`, `ProcessWeather`:\n1. Extracts `current.temperature_2m`, `current.wind_speed_10m`, and `current.weather_code` using `GET JSON ... IN PAYLOAD AS <TYPE>`.\n2. Computes Fahrenheit (`({temp_c} * 1.8) + 32`).\n3. Publishes each value to `campus/weather/reading/<field>` and then runs `PUBLISH MODEL WeatherReading TO \"campus/weather/reading\"` to emit the complete JSON object.\n\nClick **▷** on the cell below to deploy `ProcessWeather`:"
    },
    {
      "kind": 2,
      "language": "lot",
      "value": "DEFINE ACTION ProcessWeather\nON TOPIC \"campus/weather/raw\" DO\n    SET \"temp_c\" WITH (GET JSON \"current.temperature_2m\" IN PAYLOAD AS DOUBLE)\n    SET \"wind\" WITH (GET JSON \"current.wind_speed_10m\" IN PAYLOAD AS DOUBLE)\n    SET \"code\" WITH (GET JSON \"current.weather_code\" IN PAYLOAD AS INT)\n    SET \"temp_f\" WITH (({temp_c} * 1.8) + 32)\n    PUBLISH TOPIC \"campus/weather/reading/temperature_c\" WITH {temp_c}\n    PUBLISH TOPIC \"campus/weather/reading/temperature_f\" WITH {temp_f}\n    PUBLISH TOPIC \"campus/weather/reading/wind_kmh\" WITH {wind}\n    PUBLISH TOPIC \"campus/weather/reading/weather_code\" WITH {code}\n    PUBLISH MODEL WeatherReading TO \"campus/weather/reading\"\n"
    },
    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "### Test it with a sample payload\n\nBefore connecting the live weather API in Lab 3, test your Model and Action manually:\n1. Open **Data Viewer** from the **bottom Dock** and click **Publish**.\n2. Publish to topic **`campus/weather/raw`** with this JSON payload:\n\n```json\n{\"current\":{\"temperature_2m\":22.5,\"wind_speed_10m\":14.0,\"weather_code\":1}}\n```\n\n3. Click **`campus/weather/reading`** in the Data Viewer topic tree — you should see a JSON object with `temperature_c: 22.5`, `temperature_f: 72.5`, `wind_kmh: 14`, `weather_code: 1`, `station: \"campus-main\"`, and an `observed_at` UTC timestamp.\n\n**Next up:** Open **`03-campus-weather.lotnb`** to fetch live weather from Open-Meteo!"
    }
  ]
}
